    <briefdescription>
<para>A pull-based iterator whose reads may fail. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><ref refid="classiceberg_1_1Iterator" kindref="compound">Iterator</ref> implementations own any resources needed to produce values. Destroying an iterator releases those resources, including when iteration stops before reaching the end. Iterators are not thread-safe unless an implementation explicitly says otherwise. Once <ref refid="classiceberg_1_1Iterator_1a0a5d3f0cf558d9105317ea80993f96c4" kindref="member">Next()</ref> returns an error or std::nullopt, the iterator is terminal. Subsequent calls return the same terminal result without invoking the implementation again.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>T</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Value returned by the iterator. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
